{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>From the house of slaves.</b> Rashi explained: from the place where you were slaves there. And if you ask: but in the perasha of Yitro, regarding מבית עבדים, Rashi explained 'and not slaves to slaves' — one may answer, this is what it says there: or perhaps it means only from the house of slaves, that you were slaves to slaves, i.e., you were not slaves to Pharaoh but only to his servants — a scriptural inference teaches ויפדך מבית עבדים, from the hand of Pharaoh. Say from now: they were slaves to the king and not slaves to slaves; even so, He brought you out from under his hand."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:51:59.842029813Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}